# Credentials for `pnpm smoke` against sandbox-secure.zift.io.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .gitignore covers .env and .env.*; keep it that way.
# Nothing here belongs in a shell export, a commit, a pull request or a chat
# message — it is a live merchant credential even in sandbox.
#
# These three are ALL that stands between you and a working sandbox: the
# gateway rejects on credentials and nothing else. Verified 2026-09-09 — an
# unauthenticated POST answers
# `responseType=exception&responseCode=L01&responseMessage=Username or password is invalid.`

ZIFT_USERNAME=
ZIFT_PASSWORD=
ZIFT_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Optional, and together they unlock the vault and charge ladder.
#
# ZIFT_TOKEN is a proxynization token from a browser, or one returned by a
# previous sale. This script will not take a card number, so there is no other
# way to get one — see its header for why.
#
# ZIFT_ACCOUNT_ACCESSORY is the card expiry as MMYY. Zift requires it on every
# charge EVEN WHEN the card is identified by a token, which is why the schema
# keeps a column for it.
# ZIFT_TOKEN=
# ZIFT_ACCOUNT_ACCESSORY=
